              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{\mathbb{C}}
              sees only “half” of it (by
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "e-invariant#Adams66"} Adams 66, Prop. 7.14
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/24+branes+transverse+to+K3"} 24 branes transverse to K3
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres"} first stable homotopy group of spheres
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres"} second stable homotopy group of spheres
          %h2#references References
          %p The original computation:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Abramovich+Rokhlin"}> Vladimir Abramovich Rokhlin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  On a mapping of the
                  = succeed "-dimensional" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+3)
                  = succeed "-dimensional" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p with a mistake (in the unstable range) corrected in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Abramovich+Rokhlin"}> Vladimir Abramovich Rokhlin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em New results in the theory of four-dimensional manifolds
          %p French translations are in:
          %ul
            %li
              Lucien Guillou, Alexis Marin (eds.),
              = succeed "," do
                %em A la Recherche de la Topologie Perdue: I. Du côté de chez Rohlin. II. Le côté de Casson
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#WangXu10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Guozhen+Wang"}> Guozhen Wang
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zhouli+Xu"} Zhouli Xu
              = succeed "," do
                %em A survey of computations of homotopy groups of Spheres and Cobordisms
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/WangXuHomotopyGroupsOfSpheres2010.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Mehmet Kirdar,
              %em On the First, the Second and the Third Stems of the Stable Homotopy Groups of Spheres
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.06103"}> arXiv:2107.06103
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            More on the computation via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MFr"} framed cobordism ring
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-manifold"} K3-manifold
            giving the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
            that witnesses the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+of+a+group"} order
            of 24:
          %ul
            %li#Bauer10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tilman+Bauer"}> Tilman Bauer
                , answer to:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em third stable homotopy group of spheres via geometry?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/44885/381"} MO:a/44885
            %li#SP17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Schommer-Pries"}> Chris Schommer-Pries
                , answer to:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Nilpotence of the stable Hopf map via framed cobordism
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/218053/381"} MO:a/218053
          %p
            Via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/immersions"} immersions
            of 3-spheres into Euclidean 4-space
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A. Szűcs,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Two Theorems of Rokhlin
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1021208007146"} doi:10.1023/A:1021208007146
            %li
              %p
                Tobias Ekholm, Masamichi Takase,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Singular Seifert surfaces and Smale invariants for a family of 3-sphere immersions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0903.0238"} arXiv:0903.0238
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+string+structure"} geometric
            string bordism in degreee 3 as a means to speak (via the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+theorem"} Pontryagin-Thom theorem
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/third+stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres"} third stable homotopy group of spheres
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eugenio+Landi"} Eugenio Landi
                %em Integrals detecting degree 3 string cobordism classes
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.12933"}> arXiv:2209.12933
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    String bordism invariants in dimension 3 from
                    = succeed "-valued" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://nyuad.nyu.edu/en/events/2023/march/quantum-field-theories-and-cobordisms.html"} QFT and Cobordism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CQTS"} CQTS
                (Mar 2023) &amp;lbrack;
